:: Robin Bunny
<<set $outisde to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
Feeling a sudden urge, you turn towards Robin and butt your head against <<his>>.
<<if $robin.timer.hurt gte 1>>
Robin hesitates for a moment before moving your head away from <<him>>.
<<else>>
<<He>> giggles as your ears tickle <<his>> nose.
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Water Dragon
<<set $outside to 0>><<set $location to "home">><<effects>>
Feeling safe and happy as you relax with Robin, little squeaks and clicks bubble up your throat and your tail starts to wag.
Robin pauses <<his>> game to look over at you in surprise. "You sound like a dolphin!" <<he>> giggles,
and you can't help but to laugh along with <<him>>.
<br><br>
<<He>> takes a breath and attempts to replicate the sound. <<Hes>> not great at first, but you squeak and
click along with <<him>> until <<he>> almost gets the hang of it. You go back and forth for a time, enjoying the moment.
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Talk Transgender
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set _identity to playerFeltGender()>><<set _correction to $robinGenderTalk is 1>>
<<if _correction>>
	<<set $robinGenderTalk to 2>>
<<else>>
	<<set $robinGenderTalk to _identity is "n" ? 1 : 2>><<run $transgenderknown.pushUnique("Robin")>>
<</if>>
<<if _correction>>
	Robin pauses <<his>> game when you sit down. "What's wrong?"
	<br><br>
	You tell <<him>> <<he>> got it wrong. When you said your body wasn't the answer,
	<<he>> went and picked the opposite answer instead of asking you.
	<br><br>
	"Oh." <<He>> sets the controller down. "I thought that was what you meant."
<<else>>
	Robin pauses <<his>> game when you sit down. "What's wrong?"
	<br><br>
	You tell <<him>> that people look at your body, decide what you are from it, and treat everything else as dressing up.
	That being called a crossdresser stings, because you aren't wearing a costume.
	<br><br>
	Robin sets the controller down. "So you want to be the other one," <<he>> says.
	"A <<if $player.sex is "m">>girl<<else>>boy<</if>>. That's what it means, right?"
	<br><br>
	<<if _identity is "n">><<He>> says it kindly, and <<hes>> already wrong.<</if>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _identity is "f">>
	"I'm a girl," you say. "Not becoming one. I already am."
	<br><br>
	Robin takes a moment with that.
<<elseif _identity is "m">>
	"I'm a boy," you say. "Not becoming one. I already am."
	<br><br>
	Robin takes a moment with that.
<<else>>
	"I'm not a boy or a girl," you say. "Not one hiding as the other. Neither."
	<br><br>
	Robin frowns. "But there's got to be one that fits better."
	<br><br>
	"There isn't."
	<br><br>
	<<He>> doesn't argue, but <<he>> doesn't look like <<he>> follows either.
<</if>>
<br><br>
"Okay," <<he>> says. "Can I ask you something? I might ask it badly."
<br><br>
<<link [[Next|Robin Talk Transgender Body]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Talk Transgender Body
<<effects>>
Robin thinks about how to put it, and gives up on being careful.
<br><br>
"There are pills that change you," <<he>> says. "Everyone at school knows someone who's taken one.
If you took one and woke up in a body that matched, would that fix it?"
<br><br>
It's the question you've been turning over on your own.
<br><br>
<<link [[Yes. I'd take it tonight|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "yes">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[No. My body isn't what's wrong|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "no">><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[I don't know|Robin Talk Transgender End]]>><<set $robinGenderTalkBody to "unsure">><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Talk Transgender End
<<effects>>
<<set _identity to playerFeltGender()>>
<<if $robinGenderTalkBody is "yes">>
	You tell <<him>> yes. Without hesitating, and without wanting to explain why.
	<br><br>
	"Then I hope you get one," Robin says. "A good one, not the ones people hand out at parties."
<<elseif $robinGenderTalkBody is "no">>
	You tell <<him>> no. Your body isn't the thing that's wrong. What's wrong is everyone reading
	it out loud and calling that an answer.
	<br><br>
	Robin nods slowly. "So a pill wouldn't stop them. It'd just change what they decided about you."
	<br><br>
	"That's it," you say.
<<else>>
	You tell <<him>> you don't know, and that not knowing is its own kind of tiring.
	<br><br>
	"That's allowed," Robin says. "You don't have to have it worked out to be right about it."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<He>> is quiet for a while. When <<he>> speaks again <<hes>> looking at the floor.
"Bailey decides what I am. What I wear, what I'm for, what I'm called when there's money in it.
The kids at school do it too. I've never once been asked."
<br><br>
<<He>> looks up at you. "I know a bit of what that's like. Not what you're going through specifically...
just what it feels like when everyone else tries to decide who you are."
<br><br>
This is more than <<he>> usually says to you in one go.
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 70>>
	Especially then, <<he>> takes your hand. "I'll use whatever words you tell me.
	And if someone gives you trouble over it, I want to know."
	<br><br>
	At your raised eyebrow, <<he>> quickly clarifies, "To help, yes. Not to decide anything for you."
<<else>>
	Especially then, <<he>> takes your hand. "I'll use whatever words you tell me. Correct me when I get it wrong,
	I'd rather that than keep doing it."
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<if _identity is "n">>
	Robin hesitates, then gives your hand a small squeeze. The uncertainty remains on <<his>> face,
	but <<he>> stays beside you without pulling away.
<</if>>
Eventually <<he>> picks the controller back up and lets you stay beside <<him>> while <<he>> plays.
<<stress -6>><<lstress>><<npcincr Robin love 3>><<glove>><<npcincr Robin dom 2>><<gdom>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Gender Reminder
<<endevent>>
<<effects>><<npc Robin>><<person1>>
<<set $daily.robin.genderReminder to 1>>
<<if $robinGenderReminders is undefined>><<set $robinGenderReminders to 0>><</if>>
<<He>> does it again mid-sentence before, and doesn't even notice.
<br><br>
<<link [[Correct <<him>> quietly|Robin Gender Reminder Soft]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Tell <<him>> flatly to stop|Robin Gender Reminder Firm]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Let it go|Robin Gender Reminder Ignore]]>><</link>>
<br>

:: Robin Gender Reminder Soft
<<effects>>
<<set $robinGenderReminders++>>
<<set _count to $robinGenderReminders>>
You correct <<him>> gently by using the right word yourself, without turning it into a serious confrontation.
<br><br>
<<if _count lte 2>>
	Robin winces. "Which part did I get wrong?" <<he>> asks. After you tell <<him>>,
	<<he>> repeats what <<he>> meant to say, using the right word this time.
	<<npcincr Robin dom 1>><<gdom>><<stress -3>><<lstress>>
<<elseif _count lte 5>>
	Robin lowers <<his>> head and hunches slightly. "Sorry... Which part did I get wrong?"
	<br><br>
	You tell <<him>>, and <<he>> nods before starting the sentence again, using the right word this time.
	<<He>> speaks more carefully now, pausing when <<hes>> unsure rather than guessing.
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>><<stress -2>><<lstress>>
<<else>>
	Robin flinches and looks down. "Sorry. What did I say wrong?" <<he>> asks.
	<<He>> waits for you to explain before trying again.
	<br><br>
	<<Hes>> so afraid of hurting you again that <<he>> starts questioning every word before <<he>> says it.
	<<He>> uses the right words now, but often stays quiet when <<hes>> unsure.
	<<npcincr Robin dom -1>><<ldom>><<npcincr Robin trauma 1>><<grtrauma>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Gender Reminder Firm
<<effects>>
<<set $robinGenderReminders++>>
<<set _count to $robinGenderReminders>>
You tell <<him>> firmly, "Stop calling me that."
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Robin.dom gte 70>>
    Robin blinks and stops leaning back. <<He>> sits up properly, looking more serious.
	"Right," <<he>> says, nodding quickly. "I'm sorry. That's my fault."
    <br><br>
    Robin's apology sounds sincere. <<He>> looks away and stays quiet,
	clearly worried that <<he>> might say the wrong thing again.
    <<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<ldom>>
<<else>>
    Robin stops moving and stares at you, suddenly worried. "Sorry! I'm so sorry, I wasn't thinking..."
    <br><br>
    <<He>> pulls back, looking nervous. Over the next few minutes, <<he>> keeps apologising,
	even for things that have nothing to do with what happened. <<He>> seems worried that you're still angry with <<him>>.
    <<npcincr Robin dom -2>><<ldom>><<npcincr Robin trauma 2>><<grtrauma>>
<</if>>
<<if _count gte 4>>
    <br><br>
    <<Hes>> getting the words right more often now, but <<he>> still looks nervous whenever the subject comes up.
	After each sentence, <<he>> glances at your face before continuing,
	as though checking whether <<he>> said something wrong.
	<br><br>
	You've seen <<him>> act like this around Bailey when <<he>> expects to be punished.
    <<npcincr Robin love -1>><<llove>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Gender Reminder Ignore
<<effects>>
You swallow the correction, letting the wrong word pass without saying a thing.
<br><br>
<<if $robinGenderReminders gte 3>>
    It's easier this way, anyway. Lately, the exhaustion of having to correct <<him>> feels heavier than just staying quiet.
<<else>>
    The mistake stays on your mind, and you keep regretting it afterwards.
    <<stress 3>><<gstress>>
<</if>>
<br><br>
<<robinoptions>>

:: Robin Mod Widgets [widget]
<!-- Robin wakes on their own schedule and rouses the player, rather than the player guessing a wake-up hour. -->
<!-- _args[0]: "yours" if Robin climbed into your bed, "theirs" if you slept in Robin's room. -->
<<widget "robinCompanionWake">>
	<<set _robinWakeBed to _args[0]>>
	<<set _robin to statusCheck("Robin")>>
	<<endevent>>
	<<npc Robin>><<person1>>
	<<set _robinWakeRoll to random(1, 4)>>
	<<if _robin.trauma gte 50>>
		<<Hes>> already awake when you open your eyes, <<his>> arms still around you.
        "You stayed," <<he>> says. <<He>> says it like <<he>> wasn't sure you would.
		<br><br>
		<<if Time.schoolDay>>
			<<He>> looks past you at the window and sighs. "It's a school day. I suppose we should get ready."
		<<else>>
			"No school today," <<he>> says. <<He>> stays where <<he>> is a moment longer, then sits up.
		<</if>>
	<<elseif Time.schoolDay>>
		<<switch _robinWakeRoll>>
			<<case 1>>
				<<He>> shakes your shoulder until you open your eyes. "Morning," <<he>> says. "It's a school day. Let's get ready."
			<<case 2>>
				You wake to Robin already sitting up, <<his>> hair flat on one side. "Oh good, you're awake," <<he>> says. "I didn't want to go without telling you. We've got school."
			<<case 3>>
				<<He>> yawns into your shoulder, then goes still. "Wait. What day is it?" <<He>> works it out. "School. We've got school. Come on, up."
			<<default>>
				<<He>> prods your cheek until you squint at <<him>>. "Morning! Come on, we'll be late," <<he>> says, pushing the covers back.
		<</switch>>
	<<else>>
		<<switch _robinWakeRoll>>
			<<case 1>>
				<<He>> stretches beside you and yawns. "Morning," <<he>> says. "No school today. We can take our time."
			<<case 2>>
				You wake to find Robin watching you. "You scrunch your nose when you sleep," <<he>> says, then goes red. "Sorry. Morning."
			<<case 3>>
				Robin rolls over and squints at you. "Is it morning?" <<he>> asks. It is. <<He>> doesn't move for a while.
			<<default>>
				<<He>> untangles <<his>> legs from yours and sits up. "Morning," <<he>> says. "I'll see what's left for breakfast. Do you want me to bring you something?"
		<</switch>>
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if $robinromance is 1 and _robin.trauma lt 50>>
		<<He>> leans over and kisses your forehead before <<he>> swings <<his>> legs out of bed.
		<br><br>
	<</if>>
	<<if _robinWakeBed is "theirs">>
		<<He>> crosses to <<his>> wardrobe and starts picking through it. Your own clothes are back in your room.
	<<else>>
		<<He>> gathers <<his>> things, ready to slip back to <<his>> own room before anyone notices <<hes>> not in it.
	<</if>>
	<br><br>
	<<if Time.hour is 6>><<run setRobinLocationOverride("orphanage", 6)>><</if>>
	<<if _robinWakeBed is "theirs">>
		<<set $phase to 1>>
		<<endevent "phaseless">>
		<<bedicon "zzz">><<link [[Pull the covers back over yourself|Robin Bed]]>><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if $renttime lte 0>>
			<<set $bus to "home">><<set $inRobinsRoom to true>>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Get up with Robin|Bedroom Bailey]]>><<set $wardrobe_location to "wardrobe">><<set $wear_outfit to "clotheson">><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Get up with Robin|Robin Room Wake]]>><<set $wardrobe_location to "wardrobe">><<set $wear_outfit to "clotheson">><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<<else>>
		<<set $phase to 0>>
		<<endevent>>
		<<bedicon "zzz">><<link [[Pull the covers back over yourself|Bed]]>><<set $robinbed to "yours">><<set $bedGuest to "Robin">><</link>>
		<br>
		<<if $renttime lte 0>>
			<<set $bus to "home">>
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Get up with Robin|Bedroom Bailey]]>><<unset $robinbed>><<unset $bedGuest>><<set $wear_outfit to "clotheson">><</link>>
		<<else>>
			<!-- Robin heading off is already narrated above, so clear the flag Bedroom would repeat it from. -->
			<<getouticon>><<link [[Get up with Robin|Bedroom]]>><<unset $robinbed>><<unset $bedGuest>><<set $wear_outfit to "clotheson">><</link>>
		<</if>>
	<</if>>
	<br>
<</widget>>
